---
description: Decide whether the editor needs a grounded private visual packet.
args:
  goal: string
  desk: EditorDesk
  news: NewsEvidenceReport
returns: EditorPacketPlan
---
1. Check that the assigned reader reviewed the current edition and its original source bytes. Require a ready briefing and a grounded plan before making a visual packet.
2. Choose stats for supported numeric scope, checklist for explicit review gates, or timeline for dated milestones the brief can substantiate. Copy the current retained title and revision. Do not turn missing counts or speculation into visual data.
3. Require the current private draft grant, not a screenshot or an earlier authorization. When the request is review-only, record which view would fit with no effect. When coverage or authority is insufficient, hold and retain the exact reason.
